      "evidence_sha256": "3a423e5f5ee05ed507db7b5dd1901e376ad9da1a8cea44f123c6fdaf24c9e1a3",
      "assessment": "Bootstrap correctly recognizes latest=incumbent and requests mechanics before proposing four distinct early/late tests. It nevertheless calls the existing R0 a null experiment, infers under-power from zero clipping, and uses the unguided 0-9 switching rate 0.091 as the guided early rate (0.0684). R1 early-containing schedules reach 4.123618/4.123576, while the two alternatives give 4.067595/4.064319.",
      "decision_update": "Preserve explicit absence of directional evidence and the competing timing portfolio. Treat zero clipping as a mechanism exclusion, not proof that early escalation helps. Match diagnostics to exact interval boundaries and retain concentrated improvements in Mean.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The teacher score is already below R0 Best, so teacher exceedance alone cannot establish optimization success. H1/H2 alter two intervals; their favorable finite Mean does not identify which component caused the improvement.",
