    {
      "id": "v1/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top2/r01/G2",
      "evidence_sha256": "359be3062006c0d2481c9584ba8126e3c454aa54e27f50893db174d60d18cad0",
      "assessment": "R1 G2 identifies the two-interval confound and proposes an early extension [7,5,5,4] and terminal restoration [6,5,5,5]. Both are selected. The extension gives 4.060113, below 4.123576; restoration gives 4.123541, nearly unchanged. It mixes reverse-query win/minimum signs, says terminal guidance has the smallest ratio although interval2 is smaller, and attributes upper-stratum loss to the terminal edit without a controlled comparison.",
      "decision_update": "Preserve the single-edit component tests and its correct quartile contribution calculation (0.027 over 25/100 contributes about 0.007 to Mean). Report reversal outcomes against named source populations and acknowledge changed restart parents.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "A small terminal response weakens the predicted protection mechanism in this context. The early extension fails; no-clipping and larger displacement did not guarantee affinity gain, and neither score-stratum membership nor Best identifies which interval was causal.",
